# 7. INTELLIGENT MULTI-NGO DONATION ALLOCATION

This is one of the main innovations of the project.

Create an intelligent allocation system that distributes confirmed food among suitable NGOs.

Consider:
1. NGO location and service area.
2. Requested quantity.
3. Number of beneficiaries.
4. Food categories accepted.
5. NGO collection capacity.
6. Transport availability.
7. Time remaining before the safe-use deadline.
8. NGO availability.
9. Existing pending allocations.

Example:

A hotel confirms 100 meals.

NGO A requires 40 meals.
NGO B requires 35 meals.
NGO C can collect 25 meals.

The system should be able to distribute:

- NGO A: 40 meals.
- NGO B: 35 meals.
- NGO C: 25 meals.

Total allocated: 100 meals.

Include an allocation explanation showing why each NGO was selected.

Allow manual administrator intervention when needed.

IMPORTANT ALLOCATION RULES:

- Never allocate more than the confirmed quantity.
- Never allocate the same quantity twice.
- Never allocate expired or unsuitable food.
- Maintain correct remaining quantities.
- Consider food collection deadlines.
- Recalculate remaining availability after every accepted allocation.
- Keep a clear allocation history.

Show allocation as:
- Pending.
- Partially Allocated.
- Fully Allocated.
- Accepted.
- Rejected.
- Pickup Scheduled.
- Collected.
- Completed.
- Cancelled.
- Expired.
- Unclaimed.

